title: QA: password reset test cases
description: Each path through the flow is a test case. Coloured stickies are cases with expected results.
direction: down

start: Open "Forgot password" [pill, green]
email: Enter e-mail
known: Account exists? [diamond]
sent: Show "check your inbox" [rounded]
silent: Show same message\n(no account leak) [rounded]
link: Click link in e-mail
valid: Token valid & < 30 min? [diamond]
newpw: Enter new password
strong: Meets policy? [diamond]
err: Inline error [rounded, red]
ok: Logged in [pill, green]
expired: "Link expired" + resend [rounded, orange]

start -> email -> known
known -> sent: yes
known -> silent: no
sent -> link -> valid
valid -> newpw: yes
valid -> expired: no
newpw -> strong
strong -> ok: yes
strong -> err: no
err ..> newpw: retry

group cases: Test cases [gray] {
  tc1: TC-01 Happy path\nGiven known e-mail → logged in\nPriority: P0 [sticky, green]
  tc2: TC-02 Unknown e-mail\nExpect identical message\nP0 · security [sticky, yellow]
  tc3: TC-03 Expired token (31 min)\nExpect resend CTA · P1 [sticky, orange]
  tc4: TC-04 Weak password\nExpect inline error, no submit · P1 [sticky, red]
  tc5: TC-05 Token reuse\nSecond click → expired · P0 [sticky, orange]
}
tc1 .. ok [dotted]
tc2 .. silent [dotted]
tc3 .. expired [dotted]
tc4 .. err [dotted]
tc5 .. valid [dotted]

comment on tc5 by mia: Do we invalidate the token after a successful reset or after first click?
